Hello Samundra
Thanks for sending the nice study area map (pdf was just 366 Kb). I think my earlier point 3 still applies. If all detected tigers had range centres in the region you are calling "our sampling area" then you would use that as your mask when fitting the model. But you don't believe this (e.g., some Valmiki tigers probably cross the border), so you rightly use a larger mask and there is an inescapable problem computing "realised N" for "our sampling area".
Murray

