I would not expect that function to work in situ for the traps attribute of a multi-session capthist object. The argument may be a capthist or a list of traps or mask objects. Suggest you either apply to the traps objects before constructing the multisession capthist or hack the code

shareFactorLevels <- function (object, columns = NULL) {
    if (ms(object)) {
        if (!is.null(covariates(object))) {
            df <- do.call(rbind, covariates(object))
            if (is.null(columns)) columns <- 1:ncol(df)
            for (i in columns) {
                if (is.factor(df[,i])) {
                    levelsi <- levels(df[,i])
                    for (sess in 1:length(object)) {
                        covariates(object[[sess]])[,i] <-

                            factor(covariates(object[[sess]])[,i],
                                   levels = levelsi)
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    object
}

