Below is a description of some errors that occurred when I use derived() on openCR models:

It seems a little buggy when used on spatial openCR models (you need to call the estimates directly from the output list to see them, the last kappa doesn't get estimated though it does for non-spatial models, and it doesn't work with JSSAsecrbCL models - it produces the following error:

> derived(fitsecrb[[1]])
Error in makegkcpp(as.integer(nrow(realparval0)), as.integer(k), as.integer(m),  :
