In response to 1), would it be appropriate to use an individual covariate to solve this problem? My thinking would be to add habitat covariates such as the mean % forested around each animals centroid as an individual covariate. Animal 1 occupies an area, on average with 10% forest, Animal 2, with 40% forest, and so on. This would be done manually before and added into the capture history.

